\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{From a field energy to a weight}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{The weighted energy of a real field in \ref{fdip-0008} is expressed
through its pairing and [weighted Laplacian](fdip-0007).
Integration over fields also calls for a nonnegative function to
assign their relative weights. How can a linear endomorphism and
a fixed real inner product supply such a function?}
